[[:db/retract 17592186115442 :activity/steps 17592186116386] [:db/retract 17592186115442 :activity/steps 17592186116388] [:db/retract 17592186115442 :activity/steps 17592186115996] [:db/retract 17592186116386 :step/next 17592186115996] [:db/retract 17592186115996 :step/next 17592186116387] [:db/retract 17592186116388 :step/next 17592186116389] {:db/id 17592186115405 :knowledge-point/title "Solving Multi-Step Problems Involving Complementary Angles" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186114981 :question/math-academy-id "e-18993" :question/problem "In the figure below, $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles. If $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD$ and $m \\angle COB = 50^\\circ,$ find $m \\angle AOD.$\n\n![](images/60/60c48e8ce5fd289f6aa7b80cfd5a99db1adf9a0603e6162c1fb5b4dcf1a7e15d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC+m∠COB & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOC+{50}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOC & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD,$ we have\n\n$$\nm \\angle BOD = m \\angle AOC=40^\\circ .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOD & =m∠AOC+m∠COB+m∠BOD \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}+{50}^{∘}+{40}^{∘} \\\\  & ={130}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116445 :tutorial/math-academy-id 13548 :tutorial/content "**Complementary angles** are two angles whose measures have a sum of $90^\\circ,$ a right angle.\n\n![](images/27/2723049c087f5fa7b061bc9f1d4fb8c894c1e94aee3dfb994a237cd889a377e0.png)\n\nFor example, the angles in the diagram above are complementary because the sum of their measures is $90^\\circ\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n60^\\circ +30^\\circ = 90^\\circ\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" :tutorial/id #uuid "62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" :tutorial/math-academy-id 15157 :tutorial/title "Working With Diagrams" :tutorial/content "Now, consider the following diagram.\n\n![](images/02/02d8744bbc39ac9ed10d276071599f9008185023ebdfc3aaf97aebd498d82629.png)\n\nLet's solve for $x$ given the figure above.\n\nFrom the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n46^\\circ + (8x + 4^\\circ) = 90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{46}^{∘}+(8x+{4}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{50}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={40}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={5}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115442 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :activity/steps ["step-fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" "step-70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640"] :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116385 :step/math-academy-id 484813 :step/next "step-fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" :step/id #uuid "fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" :step/content 17592186503647 :step/math-academy-id 484814 :step/next "step-70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" :step/id #uuid "70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" :step/content "tutorial-62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" :step/math-academy-id 619142 :step/next 17592186116387 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116387 :step/math-academy-id 484817 :step/next 17592186116389 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116389 :step/math-academy-id 484820 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078607 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9a46b6ba-aacd-5c29-a1ea-c98b8e558d24" "question-7efd0b4a-5765-528c-b6d9-1a45ad254c36" "question-cd26c621-effc-5c15-8ae1-c10830f17e99"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a46b6ba-aacd-5c29-a1ea-c98b8e558d24" :question/id #uuid "9a46b6ba-aacd-5c29-a1ea-c98b8e558d24" :question/math-academy-id "q-47536" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b280f9756119d26317899e07e9a23b3679555701b23096516afb7a646cda453.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=5$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=5$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(5) & ≈\\frac{f(5+1)-f(5-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(6)-f(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25c0ebe2-4b2c-5787-820d-66d49ff4c628"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25c0ebe2-4b2c-5787-820d-66d49ff4c628" :answer-field/id #uuid "25c0ebe2-4b2c-5787-820d-66d49ff4c628" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3fff293c-de20-5044-b28e-7478bb356eb4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da88aa0d-3077-5d10-8f29-a83e3333cc00" "answer-3fff293c-de20-5044-b28e-7478bb356eb4" "answer-8137a3bb-83fe-54a8-93e9-dda64e173d6f" "answer-b9240be5-a3ff-50e1-956c-707b96dc2cd1" "answer-b25b775f-bf2f-5603-9f95-e4800c7215ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da88aa0d-3077-5d10-8f29-a83e3333cc00" :answer/id #uuid "da88aa0d-3077-5d10-8f29-a83e3333cc00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fff293c-de20-5044-b28e-7478bb356eb4" :answer/id #uuid "3fff293c-de20-5044-b28e-7478bb356eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8137a3bb-83fe-54a8-93e9-dda64e173d6f" :answer/id #uuid "8137a3bb-83fe-54a8-93e9-dda64e173d6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9240be5-a3ff-50e1-956c-707b96dc2cd1" :answer/id #uuid "b9240be5-a3ff-50e1-956c-707b96dc2cd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b25b775f-bf2f-5603-9f95-e4800c7215ce" :answer/id #uuid "b25b775f-bf2f-5603-9f95-e4800c7215ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078608 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eee2d2d0-57b3-5f3a-92f2-640ee03bafc1" "question-6feb34ac-08d5-5bc5-ac07-3b8f7d9f2f78"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-eee2d2d0-57b3-5f3a-92f2-640ee03bafc1" :question/id #uuid "eee2d2d0-57b3-5f3a-92f2-640ee03bafc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-51403" :question/problem "The population growth of a developing rural area was studied for $25$ years. The following table shows the population $p(t),$ in hundreds, recorded $t$ years after $1990.$\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p(t)$ | $90$ | $98$ | $116$ | $138$ | $178$ | $220$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the population growth rate in the year $2005$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=5.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{p}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{p(t+h)-p(t-h)}{2h}.\n$$\n\n \nWe note that year $2005$ corresponds to $t=15.$ The step size is $h=5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(15) & ≈\\frac{p(15+5)-p(15-5)}{2(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{p(20)-p(10)}{2(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{178-116}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{62}{10} \\\\  & =6.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the population growth rate in $2005$ was $620$ people per year." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0af4d3cf-e65d-5887-a3c8-fbf3cb5968a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0af4d3cf-e65d-5887-a3c8-fbf3cb5968a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "0af4d3cf-e65d-5887-a3c8-fbf3cb5968a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4b289394-f864-5590-bd44-39400c5b19de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66768288-36bc-5a05-a7d0-09dc524837bc" "answer-697d63fe-7536-5001-b451-eef387f2b71b" "answer-4b289394-f864-5590-bd44-39400c5b19de" "answer-3b3be121-1868-5c15-bb39-9dc444f96c37" "answer-42d87068-7c26-500b-86bd-276963ea2b56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66768288-36bc-5a05-a7d0-09dc524837bc" :answer/id #uuid "66768288-36bc-5a05-a7d0-09dc524837bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$220$ people per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-697d63fe-7536-5001-b451-eef387f2b71b" :answer/id #uuid "697d63fe-7536-5001-b451-eef387f2b71b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$400$ people per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b289394-f864-5590-bd44-39400c5b19de" :answer/id #uuid "4b289394-f864-5590-bd44-39400c5b19de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$620$ people per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b3be121-1868-5c15-bb39-9dc444f96c37" :answer/id #uuid "3b3be121-1868-5c15-bb39-9dc444f96c37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$800$ people per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42d87068-7c26-500b-86bd-276963ea2b56" :answer/id #uuid "42d87068-7c26-500b-86bd-276963ea2b56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$820$ people per year" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7efd0b4a-5765-528c-b6d9-1a45ad254c36" :question/id #uuid "7efd0b4a-5765-528c-b6d9-1a45ad254c36" :question/math-academy-id "q-75127" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b76466e577343a234b53566b00939a3de312ad4f71106ebf3cbed3bc9d8795ea.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=8$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=8$ with step size $h=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(8) & ≈\\frac{f(8+4)-f(8-4)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(12)-f(4)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-6}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4575b9d0-3088-5690-8faf-edd6c5589e6b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4575b9d0-3088-5690-8faf-edd6c5589e6b" :answer-field/id #uuid "4575b9d0-3088-5690-8faf-edd6c5589e6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-21dcbd9a-b189-5e6a-bc35-a6c210cd27cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd8c286e-5853-5464-a9a1-bab70973849c" "answer-21dcbd9a-b189-5e6a-bc35-a6c210cd27cb" "answer-388f9860-936a-5e7e-b68f-0a73360204b3" "answer-7834e1cb-c346-5829-b413-979630b7caca" "answer-90b975cc-2770-51d1-9c1f-ed99aaf7a2fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd8c286e-5853-5464-a9a1-bab70973849c" :answer/id #uuid "cd8c286e-5853-5464-a9a1-bab70973849c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21dcbd9a-b189-5e6a-bc35-a6c210cd27cb" :answer/id #uuid "21dcbd9a-b189-5e6a-bc35-a6c210cd27cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-388f9860-936a-5e7e-b68f-0a73360204b3" :answer/id #uuid "388f9860-936a-5e7e-b68f-0a73360204b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7834e1cb-c346-5829-b413-979630b7caca" :answer/id #uuid "7834e1cb-c346-5829-b413-979630b7caca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90b975cc-2770-51d1-9c1f-ed99aaf7a2fb" :answer/id #uuid "90b975cc-2770-51d1-9c1f-ed99aaf7a2fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cd26c621-effc-5c15-8ae1-c10830f17e99" :question/id #uuid "cd26c621-effc-5c15-8ae1-c10830f17e99" :question/math-academy-id "q-344028" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bfc66c5e19ff0fe88cba465c6b045402fc5f8753befa4acb3b1cc3839acf8a7.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=2$ and $x=4.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(3)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+1)-f(3-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4)-f(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-edd45b2c-b238-5306-8bee-cea5535e0e17"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-edd45b2c-b238-5306-8bee-cea5535e0e17" :answer-field/id #uuid "edd45b2c-b238-5306-8bee-cea5535e0e17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-61dafa90-cdc3-5f41-91ad-f2638de3936e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61dafa90-cdc3-5f41-91ad-f2638de3936e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61dafa90-cdc3-5f41-91ad-f2638de3936e" :answer/id #uuid "61dafa90-cdc3-5f41-91ad-f2638de3936e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6feb34ac-08d5-5bc5-ac07-3b8f7d9f2f78" :question/id #uuid "6feb34ac-08d5-5bc5-ac07-3b8f7d9f2f78" :question/math-academy-id "q-344354" :question/problem "In a physics experiment, the net charge on a sensor (in $mC$) after $t$ seconds is given by the function $Q(t).$ The values of $Q(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1.0$ | $1.5$ | $2.0$ | $2.5$ | $3.0$ | $3.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$Q(t)$** | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |\n\nApproximate the sensor’s charge instantaneous rate of change at $t=2.5$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.5.$\n\nThe sensor’s charge at $t=2.5$ is decreasing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $mC$ per second." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{Q}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{Q(t+h)-Q(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=2.5$ with step size $h=0.5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{′}(2.5) & ≈\\frac{Q(2.5+0.5)-Q(2.5-0.5)}{2(0.5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{Q(3.0)-Q(2.0)}{1.0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-2}{1.0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{1.0} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sensor’s charge at $t=2.5$ is decreasing at approximately $3\\,mC$ per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e65356f5-f20f-5d3d-9cec-00adbcee6de3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e65356f5-f20f-5d3d-9cec-00adbcee6de3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e65356f5-f20f-5d3d-9cec-00adbcee6de3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-09c0fbb2-7164-5851-b930-a2535a1ccb70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09c0fbb2-7164-5851-b930-a2535a1ccb70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09c0fbb2-7164-5851-b930-a2535a1ccb70" :answer/id #uuid "09c0fbb2-7164-5851-b930-a2535a1ccb70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fc6b7687-cfeb-5f5f-a997-e613e67ace2c" :activity/id #uuid "fc6b7687-cfeb-5f5f-a997-e613e67ace2c" :activity/title "Estimating Derivatives Using a Central Difference Quotient" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049111 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-837165f8-c967-55f3-b235-24e13a193e14" "step-75e3868f-a25b-5151-8a0c-5be1318bc937" "step-ef594372-6cb5-54ca-9621-701e5b7ba954" "step-1a14f9f1-1b0f-594d-a6d2-e0a52c7322ee" "step-c47052fd-5450-5904-80f3-546487c65903"] :activity/first-step "step-837165f8-c967-55f3-b235-24e13a193e14" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-837165f8-c967-55f3-b235-24e13a193e14" :step/id #uuid "837165f8-c967-55f3-b235-24e13a193e14" :step/content "question-9a46b6ba-aacd-5c29-a1ea-c98b8e558d24" :step/next "step-75e3868f-a25b-5151-8a0c-5be1318bc937" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-75e3868f-a25b-5151-8a0c-5be1318bc937" :step/id #uuid "75e3868f-a25b-5151-8a0c-5be1318bc937" :step/content "question-eee2d2d0-57b3-5f3a-92f2-640ee03bafc1" :step/next "step-ef594372-6cb5-54ca-9621-701e5b7ba954" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ef594372-6cb5-54ca-9621-701e5b7ba954" :step/id #uuid "ef594372-6cb5-54ca-9621-701e5b7ba954" :step/content "question-7efd0b4a-5765-528c-b6d9-1a45ad254c36" :step/next "step-1a14f9f1-1b0f-594d-a6d2-e0a52c7322ee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1a14f9f1-1b0f-594d-a6d2-e0a52c7322ee" :step/id #uuid "1a14f9f1-1b0f-594d-a6d2-e0a52c7322ee" :step/content "question-cd26c621-effc-5c15-8ae1-c10830f17e99" :step/next "step-c47052fd-5450-5904-80f3-546487c65903" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c47052fd-5450-5904-80f3-546487c65903" :step/id #uuid "c47052fd-5450-5904-80f3-546487c65903" :step/content "question-6feb34ac-08d5-5bc5-ac07-3b8f7d9f2f78" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186185598 :answer-field/choices 17592186185600] [:db/retract 17592186185598 :answer-field/choices 17592186185601] [:db/retract 17592186185598 :answer-field/choices 17592186185602] [:db/retract 17592186185598 :answer-field/choices 17592186185603] [:db/retract 17592186185598 :answer-field/choices 17592186185599] [:db/retract 17592186185628 :answer-field/choices 17592186185632] [:db/retract 17592186185628 :answer-field/choices 17592186185633] [:db/retract 17592186185628 :answer-field/choices 17592186185629] [:db/retract 17592186185628 :answer-field/choices 17592186185630] [:db/retract 17592186185628 :answer-field/choices 17592186185631] {:db/id 17592186188553 :question/problem "Consider a sample of size $n=64$ from a population. Given that the sample mean is $60,$ and the sample standard deviation is $24,$ find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>2.656)=0.005,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $63$ degrees of freedom.*" :question/worked-solution "We do not know the distribution of the population, nor do we know the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ However, the sample size $n=64\\ge 30$ is *sufficiently large*. \n\nIn cases like this, the random variable\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{S/\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated by the student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{n-1}$ with $n-1$ degrees of freedom, where \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${S}^{2}$ is the sample variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(T>{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ and $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1$ degrees of freedom.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=60,\\,n=64,\\,s=24.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $99%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.99=0.01\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.005.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>2.656)=0.005.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}={t}_{63,0.005}=2.656.\n$$\n\n![](images/55/5596a286f89b2eed9fd6340c00e77915f84883f2d57d1b342b762143811537aa.png)\n\nTherefore, the $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60 & \\pm 2.656\\cdot \\frac{24}{\\sqrt{64}} \\\\ 60 & \\pm 7.968\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185598 :answer-field/correct "answer-09003a28-3717-5e7f-9baa-237b32a73563" :answer-field/choices ["answer-066610ff-3d82-50b2-b812-1338bebdf1d1" "answer-84f0eeaf-ad7b-52c3-b682-813bce3f605f" "answer-06c2f12e-68a5-528e-9841-ad944de82b35" "answer-34abe2f4-dc85-5332-b992-cc39f815e618" "answer-09003a28-3717-5e7f-9baa-237b32a73563"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-066610ff-3d82-50b2-b812-1338bebdf1d1" :answer/id #uuid "066610ff-3d82-50b2-b812-1338bebdf1d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\pm 2.576" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84f0eeaf-ad7b-52c3-b682-813bce3f605f" :answer/id #uuid "84f0eeaf-ad7b-52c3-b682-813bce3f605f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\pm 5.221" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06c2f12e-68a5-528e-9841-ad944de82b35" :answer/id #uuid "06c2f12e-68a5-528e-9841-ad944de82b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60\\pm 1.288" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34abe2f4-dc85-5332-b992-cc39f815e618" :answer/id #uuid "34abe2f4-dc85-5332-b992-cc39f815e618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60\\pm 2.576" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09003a28-3717-5e7f-9baa-237b32a73563" :answer/id #uuid "09003a28-3717-5e7f-9baa-237b32a73563" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60\\pm 7.968" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188558 :question/problem "Consider a sample of size $n=100$ from a population. Given that the sample mean is $252,$ and the sample standard deviation is $81,$ find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>1.984)=0.025,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $99$ degrees of freedom.*" :question/worked-solution "We do not know the distribution of the population, nor do we know the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ However, the sample size $n=100\\ge 30$ is *sufficiently large*. \n\nIn cases like this, the random variable\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{S/\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated by the student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{n-1}$ with $n-1$ degrees of freedom, where \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${S}^{2}$ is the sample variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(T>{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ and $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1$ degrees of freedom.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=252,\\,n=100,\\,s=81.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $95%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.95=0.05\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(T>1.984)=0.025.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}={t}_{99,0.025}=1.984.\n$$\n\n![](images/5b/5b33840d7c98bbf799bdc58dc90d84752b3fa84c36d4a9b122a20ec9401b6823.png)\n\nTherefore, the $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}252 & \\pm 1.984\\cdot \\frac{81}{\\sqrt{100}} \\\\ 252 & \\pm 16.070\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185628 :answer-field/correct "answer-dd26c9b8-8eb6-53aa-bf47-535a91ee6396" :answer-field/choices ["answer-247effcb-626c-5ae3-bd39-1910118941fa" "answer-d9a7ad11-1129-5b22-9704-503871bfe339" "answer-e14ec158-b428-5af8-9f36-458c932a5ea0" "answer-dd26c9b8-8eb6-53aa-bf47-535a91ee6396" "answer-d3b4e3e8-d9aa-5bcf-bbe3-dae6af3e90a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-247effcb-626c-5ae3-bd39-1910118941fa" :answer/id #uuid "247effcb-626c-5ae3-bd39-1910118941fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "126\\pm 14.048" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9a7ad11-1129-5b22-9704-503871bfe339" :answer/id #uuid "d9a7ad11-1129-5b22-9704-503871bfe339" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "171\\pm 15.339" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e14ec158-b428-5af8-9f36-458c932a5ea0" :answer/id #uuid "e14ec158-b428-5af8-9f36-458c932a5ea0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "252\\pm 14.055" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd26c9b8-8eb6-53aa-bf47-535a91ee6396" :answer/id #uuid "dd26c9b8-8eb6-53aa-bf47-535a91ee6396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "252\\pm 16.070" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3b4e3e8-d9aa-5bcf-bbe3-dae6af3e90a3" :answer/id #uuid "d3b4e3e8-d9aa-5bcf-bbe3-dae6af3e90a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "99\\pm 8.040" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188284 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-33652587-e008-57dc-9a3a-905f5c4ae6f4" "question-bb725276-ca73-5e90-be79-e741b1537c3e" "question-969c1777-ec8b-5e40-b43c-413b46fc477f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-33652587-e008-57dc-9a3a-905f5c4ae6f4" :question/id #uuid "33652587-e008-57dc-9a3a-905f5c4ae6f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-142975" :question/problem "In a particular state, $400$ randomly selected working adults were asked the distance from their home to their workplace. The sample mean distance was $8.52\\,\\text{mi}$ with standard deviation $2.40\\,\\text{mi}.$ Find a $99%$ confidence interval for the mean distance from home to work  $\\mu $ for all working adults in this state.   \n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores ${t}_{k,p}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{k,p})=p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p.$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $398$ | $\\,1.284\\,$ | $\\,1.649\\,$ | $\\,1.966\\,$ | $\\,2.336\\,$ | $\\,2.588\\,$ |\n| $399$ | $\\,1.284\\,$ | $\\,1.649\\,$ | $\\,1.966\\,$ | $\\,2.336\\,$ | $\\,2.588\\,$ |\n| $400$ | $\\,1.284\\,$ | $\\,1.649\\,$ | $\\,1.966\\,$ | $\\,2.336\\,$ | $\\,2.588\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We do not know the distribution of the population, nor do we know the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ However, the sample size $n=400\\ge 30$ is *sufficiently large*.  \n\nIn cases like this, the random variable\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{S/\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\ncan be approximated by the student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{n-1}$ with $n-1$ degrees of freedom, where \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${S}^{2}$ is the sample variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(T>{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ and $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1$ degrees of freedom.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=8.52\\,\\text{mi},\\,n=400,\\,s=2.40\\,\\text{mi}.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $99%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.99=0.01\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.005.\n$$\n\nWe also need to find the $t$-score value ${t}_{399,0.005}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{399,0.005})=0.005,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1=400-1=399$ degrees of freedom.\n\n![](images/82/829fa68b18545ff59ffa702fe4567997d635089edf4e90d713b1c8d817c7959f.png)\n\nFrom the percentage points table of the $t$-distribution, we obtain that ${t}_{399,0.005}=2.588:$ \n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $398$ | $\\,1.284\\,$ | $\\,1.649\\,$ | $\\,1.966\\,$ | $\\,2.336\\,$ | $\\,2.588\\,$ |\n| $399$ | $\\,1.284\\,$ | $\\,1.649\\,$ | $\\,1.966\\,$ | $\\,2.336\\,$ | $2.588$ |\n| $400$ | $\\,1.284\\,$ | $\\,1.649\\,$ | $\\,1.966\\,$ | $\\,2.336\\,$ | $\\,2.588\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, the $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8.52 & \\pm 2.588\\cdot \\frac{2.40}{\\sqrt{400}}\\,\\text{mi} \\\\ 8.52 & \\pm 0.311\\,\\text{mi}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-31fb2a2b-85f8-5174-8f8c-064217a8d0bc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-31fb2a2b-85f8-5174-8f8c-064217a8d0bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "31fb2a2b-85f8-5174-8f8c-064217a8d0bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76d7e595-409f-5d32-9911-9eac076c3663" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf2957a5-69d2-53f1-a6dd-b37bfb959fc8" "answer-256f968b-f149-5a64-b5e7-35483cba2ed4" "answer-6561e4f2-6b4f-5178-9f7d-90b9b8551b65" "answer-4d4ed279-f589-55a4-9518-10e65b24f391" "answer-76d7e595-409f-5d32-9911-9eac076c3663"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf2957a5-69d2-53f1-a6dd-b37bfb959fc8" :answer/id #uuid "bf2957a5-69d2-53f1-a6dd-b37bfb959fc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.92\\pm 0.311\\,\\text{mi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-256f968b-f149-5a64-b5e7-35483cba2ed4" :answer/id #uuid "256f968b-f149-5a64-b5e7-35483cba2ed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.40\\pm 0.131\\,\\text{mi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6561e4f2-6b4f-5178-9f7d-90b9b8551b65" :answer/id #uuid "6561e4f2-6b4f-5178-9f7d-90b9b8551b65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "400\\pm 0.113\\,\\text{mi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d4ed279-f589-55a4-9518-10e65b24f391" :answer/id #uuid "4d4ed279-f589-55a4-9518-10e65b24f391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.52\\pm 0.133\\,\\text{mi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76d7e595-409f-5d32-9911-9eac076c3663" :answer/id #uuid "76d7e595-409f-5d32-9911-9eac076c3663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.52\\pm 0.311\\,\\text{mi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bb725276-ca73-5e90-be79-e741b1537c3e" :question/id #uuid "bb725276-ca73-5e90-be79-e741b1537c3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-142976" :question/problem "The amount of hemoglobin in the bloodstream of people living in a particular Colorado community follows a normal distribution. An analysis on a random sample of $16$ people yields a mean hemoglobin concentration of $13.1\\,\\text{g/dl}$ with a sample standard deviation of $1.8\\,\\text{g/dl}.$ Find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean hemoglobin concentration $\\mu $ for all people in the community.  \n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores ${t}_{k,p}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{k,p})=p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p.$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.576$ | $2.898$ |" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the population is normally distributed, but we do not know the population variance $\\sigma .$\n\nIn cases like this, the random variable\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{S/\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nfollows a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{n-1}$ with $n-1$ degrees of freedom, where\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${S}^{2}$ is the sample variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(T>{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ and $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1$ degrees of freedom.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=13.1\\,\\text{g/dl},\\,n=16,\\,s=1.8\\,\\text{g/dl}.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $95%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.95=0.05\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe also need to find the $t$-score value ${t}_{15,0.025}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{15,0.025})=0.025,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1=16-1=15$ degrees of freedom.\n\n![](images/03/03b3b3aec86ef22237d0013b3496993ae4cdda192540fc1c29f01ad608fcb810.png)\n\nFrom the percentage points table of the $t$-distribution, we obtain that ${t}_{15,0.025}=2.131:$ \n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.576$ | $2.898$ |\n\nTherefore, a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13.1 & \\pm 2.131\\cdot \\frac{1.8}{\\sqrt{16}}\\,\\text{g/dl} \\\\ 13.1 & \\pm 0.959\\,\\text{g/dl}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce4236eb-539a-5a14-a293-5eda94e5a9e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce4236eb-539a-5a14-a293-5eda94e5a9e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce4236eb-539a-5a14-a293-5eda94e5a9e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9a012243-783b-5fcd-a20c-31d094c51f1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7a652d0-3e8f-5aee-82bd-bf86b31f4084" "answer-9a012243-783b-5fcd-a20c-31d094c51f1f" "answer-f176a196-bce3-51df-8b5e-2c12622bc68c" "answer-0d97057b-a0ed-5cd4-a152-34da488534bc" "answer-a711e61d-7f5c-5a9e-a2ea-31ecb7333dbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7a652d0-3e8f-5aee-82bd-bf86b31f4084" :answer/id #uuid "c7a652d0-3e8f-5aee-82bd-bf86b31f4084" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8\\pm 1.995\\,\\text{g/dl}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a012243-783b-5fcd-a20c-31d094c51f1f" :answer/id #uuid "9a012243-783b-5fcd-a20c-31d094c51f1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13.1\\pm 0.959\\,\\text{g/dl}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f176a196-bce3-51df-8b5e-2c12622bc68c" :answer/id #uuid "f176a196-bce3-51df-8b5e-2c12622bc68c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13.1\\pm 2.131\\,\\text{g/dl}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d97057b-a0ed-5cd4-a152-34da488534bc" :answer/id #uuid "0d97057b-a0ed-5cd4-a152-34da488534bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14.9\\pm 1.959\\,\\text{g/dl}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a711e61d-7f5c-5a9e-a2ea-31ecb7333dbc" :answer/id #uuid "a711e61d-7f5c-5a9e-a2ea-31ecb7333dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\pm 0.995\\,\\text{g/dl}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-969c1777-ec8b-5e40-b43c-413b46fc477f" :question/id #uuid "969c1777-ec8b-5e40-b43c-413b46fc477f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143028" :question/problem "A tire manufacturer measures the stopping distance of a new tire model from $50\\,\\text{mph},$ on a standard test car. A sample of $25$ stopping distances yielded a sample mean of $174\\,\\text{ft}$ with a sample standard deviation of $4\\,\\text{ft}.$ Assuming that the stopping distances are normally distributed, find a $90%$ confidence interval for the mean stopping distance $\\mu $ of these tires.   \n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores ${t}_{k,p}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{k,p})=p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p.$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $23$ | $\\,1.319\\,$ | $\\,1.714\\,$ | $\\,2.069\\,$ | $\\,2.500\\,$ | $\\,2.807\\,$ |\n| $24$ | $\\,1.318\\,$ | $\\,1.711\\,$ | $\\,2.064\\,$ | $\\,2.492\\,$ | $\\,2.797\\,$ |\n| $25$ | $\\,1.316\\,$ | $\\,1.708\\,$ | $\\,2.060\\,$ | $\\,2.485\\,$ | $\\,2.787\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the population is normally distributed, but we do not know the population variance $\\sigma .$\n\nIn cases like this, the random variable\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{S/\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nfollows a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{n-1}$ with $n-1$ degrees of freedom, where\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${S}^{2}$ is the sample variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(T>{t}_{n-1,\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2},$ and $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1$ degrees of freedom.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=174\\,\\text{ft},\\,n=25,\\,s=4\\,\\text{ft}.\n$$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $90%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.9=0.1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.05.\n$$\n\nWe also need to find the $t$-score value ${t}_{24,0.05}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{24,0.05})=0.05,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $n-1=25-1=24$ degrees of freedom.\n\n![](images/52/52426e7ca1868359b5ed5c97ba1fabeaebb22b73393918d5b9031c8c6320a300.png)\n\nFrom the percentage points table of the $t$-distribution, we obtain that ${t}_{24,0.05}=1.711:$ \n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $23$ | $\\,1.319\\,$ | $\\,1.714\\,$ | $\\,2.069\\,$ | $\\,2.500\\,$ | $\\,2.807\\,$ |\n| $24$ | $\\,1.318\\,$ | $1.711$ | $\\,2.064\\,$ | $\\,2.492\\,$ | $\\,2.797\\,$ |\n| $25$ | $\\,1.316\\,$ | $\\,1.708\\,$ | $\\,2.060\\,$ | $\\,2.485\\,$ | $\\,2.787\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, a $90%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}174 & \\pm 1.711\\cdot \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{25}}\\,\\text{ft} \\\\ 174 & \\pm 1.369\\,\\text{ft}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-04f3a275-b656-5d6f-8b7c-3bd7e106dfd5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-04f3a275-b656-5d6f-8b7c-3bd7e106dfd5" :answer-field/id #uuid "04f3a275-b656-5d6f-8b7c-3bd7e106dfd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7c6a617b-52cd-5f5b-a837-7d8fa3497d1b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d1d33fe-8836-5ceb-9e21-dde0f49573e2" "answer-0eb32a81-2dc3-50ed-840b-da7ac0d69d8a" "answer-7c6a617b-52cd-5f5b-a837-7d8fa3497d1b" "answer-311561ec-4176-5648-a42d-bd951c43964d" "answer-f3605f82-ef49-559d-a1ce-7456d966fa96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d1d33fe-8836-5ceb-9e21-dde0f49573e2" :answer/id #uuid "4d1d33fe-8836-5ceb-9e21-dde0f49573e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "174\\pm 0.542\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0eb32a81-2dc3-50ed-840b-da7ac0d69d8a" :answer/id #uuid "0eb32a81-2dc3-50ed-840b-da7ac0d69d8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "174\\pm 1.084\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c6a617b-52cd-5f5b-a837-7d8fa3497d1b" :answer/id #uuid "7c6a617b-52cd-5f5b-a837-7d8fa3497d1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "174\\pm 1.369\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-311561ec-4176-5648-a42d-bd951c43964d" :answer/id #uuid "311561ec-4176-5648-a42d-bd951c43964d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\pm 1.356\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3605f82-ef49-559d-a1ce-7456d966fa96" :answer/id #uuid "f3605f82-ef49-559d-a1ce-7456d966fa96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\pm 1.084\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-34aeab81-66dd-5a0b-8751-468cd63a1098" :activity/id #uuid "34aeab81-66dd-5a0b-8751-468cd63a1098" :activity/title "Confidence Intervals for One Mean: Unknown Population Variance" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048944 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-43e3e0c5-16b5-54b6-97d1-904aec98a411" "step-29756d50-cfb9-5aeb-ab06-3e56c10fad83" "step-10d5d17f-5e05-568d-892a-89daf97c2f8d" "step-fc2ed12d-6e0a-50a2-84a6-8decfa5fc1ae" "step-f75b345d-27d5-5c91-b2b0-43c6291fee8a"] :activity/first-step "step-43e3e0c5-16b5-54b6-97d1-904aec98a411" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-43e3e0c5-16b5-54b6-97d1-904aec98a411" :step/id #uuid "43e3e0c5-16b5-54b6-97d1-904aec98a411" :step/content 17592186188553 :step/next "step-29756d50-cfb9-5aeb-ab06-3e56c10fad83" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-29756d50-cfb9-5aeb-ab06-3e56c10fad83" :step/id #uuid "29756d50-cfb9-5aeb-ab06-3e56c10fad83" :step/content 17592186188558 :step/next "step-10d5d17f-5e05-568d-892a-89daf97c2f8d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-10d5d17f-5e05-568d-892a-89daf97c2f8d" :step/id #uuid "10d5d17f-5e05-568d-892a-89daf97c2f8d" :step/content "question-33652587-e008-57dc-9a3a-905f5c4ae6f4" :step/next "step-fc2ed12d-6e0a-50a2-84a6-8decfa5fc1ae" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fc2ed12d-6e0a-50a2-84a6-8decfa5fc1ae" :step/id #uuid "fc2ed12d-6e0a-50a2-84a6-8decfa5fc1ae" :step/content "question-bb725276-ca73-5e90-be79-e741b1537c3e" :step/next "step-f75b345d-27d5-5c91-b2b0-43c6291fee8a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f75b345d-27d5-5c91-b2b0-43c6291fee8a" :step/id #uuid "f75b345d-27d5-5c91-b2b0-43c6291fee8a" :step/content "question-969c1777-ec8b-5e40-b43c-413b46fc477f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4be9a2f5-2f4a-5a28-99ac-bf9fd6c5ffaf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4be9a2f5-2f4a-5a28-99ac-bf9fd6c5ffaf" :question/id #uuid "4be9a2f5-2f4a-5a28-99ac-bf9fd6c5ffaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-60088" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d4fc837b149453ef874950260279781e57ca398b92023e28ebe4fb3b841c311.png)\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing numbers in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of rectangles to kites is $2:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ rectangles for every $5$ kites." :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of rectangles to the number of kites as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of rectangles}:\\text{number of kites}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of rectangles. There are $2$ rectangles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of kites. There are $5$ kites.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of rectangles to kites is $2:5.$\n\nTherefore, the missing numbers are $5$ and $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ae34d415-ccc8-5608-abcb-26fa7f2fa29a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ae34d415-ccc8-5608-abcb-26fa7f2fa29a" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae34d415-ccc8-5608-abcb-26fa7f2fa29a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d31ab7c6-4994-5471-beb0-1b8ac5139ddd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1e479e53-8494-57eb-96f8-9ac771475ceb" "answer-c7d42562-52c2-5c3e-9214-a27acb95bf22" "answer-d31ab7c6-4994-5471-beb0-1b8ac5139ddd" "answer-5c3cefc9-3d90-5e7d-8e1a-5a464d800db6" "answer-8fd633a8-8523-5e91-a3cc-48af3aae1d72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e479e53-8494-57eb-96f8-9ac771475ceb" :answer/id #uuid "1e479e53-8494-57eb-96f8-9ac771475ceb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7d42562-52c2-5c3e-9214-a27acb95bf22" :answer/id #uuid "c7d42562-52c2-5c3e-9214-a27acb95bf22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ and $7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d31ab7c6-4994-5471-beb0-1b8ac5139ddd" :answer/id #uuid "d31ab7c6-4994-5471-beb0-1b8ac5139ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c3cefc9-3d90-5e7d-8e1a-5a464d800db6" :answer/id #uuid "5c3cefc9-3d90-5e7d-8e1a-5a464d800db6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ and $7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fd633a8-8523-5e91-a3cc-48af3aae1d72" :answer/id #uuid "8fd633a8-8523-5e91-a3cc-48af3aae1d72" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064230 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57848bee-3e72-5d15-a97c-92bd970ffedc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-57848bee-3e72-5d15-a97c-92bd970ffedc" :question/id #uuid "57848bee-3e72-5d15-a97c-92bd970ffedc" :question/math-academy-id "q-99753" :question/problem "What is $0÷(-\\frac{8}{21})?$" :question/worked-solution "Zero divided by any number (other than zero) equals zero. Therefore, \n\n$$\n0÷(-\\frac{8}{21})=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-740f5659-04b8-5006-82f4-2605026e1fc3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-740f5659-04b8-5006-82f4-2605026e1fc3" :answer-field/id #uuid "740f5659-04b8-5006-82f4-2605026e1fc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b35bbdff-1376-5898-ab4b-cfff11b72c47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2a7853a-28a8-54cd-8b7e-385d6189ab0e" "answer-445dc765-fffa-5c9c-8032-001531d309ec" "answer-b35bbdff-1376-5898-ab4b-cfff11b72c47" "answer-7c75d6e2-200f-56c9-be87-9792e2c68716" "answer-a1dd6c8f-7899-5358-a311-16926a65bd02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2a7853a-28a8-54cd-8b7e-385d6189ab0e" :answer/id #uuid "a2a7853a-28a8-54cd-8b7e-385d6189ab0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-445dc765-fffa-5c9c-8032-001531d309ec" :answer/id #uuid "445dc765-fffa-5c9c-8032-001531d309ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b35bbdff-1376-5898-ab4b-cfff11b72c47" :answer/id #uuid "b35bbdff-1376-5898-ab4b-cfff11b72c47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c75d6e2-200f-56c9-be87-9792e2c68716" :answer/id #uuid "7c75d6e2-200f-56c9-be87-9792e2c68716" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1dd6c8f-7899-5358-a311-16926a65bd02" :answer/id #uuid "a1dd6c8f-7899-5358-a311-16926a65bd02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171934 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4d3c9434-4ef2-5a17-95da-683191ed9ce8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d3c9434-4ef2-5a17-95da-683191ed9ce8" :question/id #uuid "4d3c9434-4ef2-5a17-95da-683191ed9ce8" :question/math-academy-id "q-223451" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $631$\n\nII. $782$\n\nIII. $686$" :question/worked-solution "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $631,$ we have that \n\n$$\n63-2(1)=63-2=61\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $631$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $782,$ we have that \n\n$$\n78-2(2)=78-4=74\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $782$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $686,$ we have that \n\n$$\n68-2(6)=68-12=56\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $686$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-da0cc54c-5334-583d-91ac-093122073d60"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-da0cc54c-5334-583d-91ac-093122073d60" :answer-field/id #uuid "da0cc54c-5334-583d-91ac-093122073d60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f99d86fe-18dc-5ab3-b1d5-cc194710dad4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e74e918-bf7e-51d4-b025-37cf39ae58bb" "answer-cb8ba310-7b83-5c1c-b220-d8e14288b80b" "answer-01148fdd-b3c2-58c3-bd64-bc7039e3aa72" "answer-ca3c4587-fd47-5a07-9f96-490c2058ad00" "answer-f99d86fe-18dc-5ab3-b1d5-cc194710dad4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e74e918-bf7e-51d4-b025-37cf39ae58bb" :answer/id #uuid "7e74e918-bf7e-51d4-b025-37cf39ae58bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and  II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb8ba310-7b83-5c1c-b220-d8e14288b80b" :answer/id #uuid "cb8ba310-7b83-5c1c-b220-d8e14288b80b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01148fdd-b3c2-58c3-bd64-bc7039e3aa72" :answer/id #uuid "01148fdd-b3c2-58c3-bd64-bc7039e3aa72" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and  III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca3c4587-fd47-5a07-9f96-490c2058ad00" :answer/id #uuid "ca3c4587-fd47-5a07-9f96-490c2058ad00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f99d86fe-18dc-5ab3-b1d5-cc194710dad4" :answer/id #uuid "f99d86fe-18dc-5ab3-b1d5-cc194710dad4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147544 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3e597010-3568-5f92-b7bf-8866f8549553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3e597010-3568-5f92-b7bf-8866f8549553" :question/id #uuid "3e597010-3568-5f92-b7bf-8866f8549553" :question/math-academy-id "q-350258" :question/problem "Ethan and Lucas are swimmers. In the previous season, $75%$ of Ethan’s races were freestyle, while the decimal proportion of Lucas’s races that were freestyle was $0.4.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Ethan's races were freestyle.\n\nII. More than half of Lucas's races were freestyle.\n\nIII. Ethan had a greater percentage of freestyle races compared to Lucas." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n75%>50%,\n$$\n\nmore than half of Ethan's races were freestyle.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.4<0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of Lucas's races were freestyle.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $75%$ and $0.4$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.4\\times 100=40%\n$$\n\nSince $75%>40%,$ Ethan had a **greater** percentage of freestyle races compared to Lucas.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54b448ba-1dea-5e80-9afc-9ef26eb406f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54b448ba-1dea-5e80-9afc-9ef26eb406f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "54b448ba-1dea-5e80-9afc-9ef26eb406f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8bd1beb1-7b8d-5ba2-ad28-8ad264935383" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1905c358-05c8-5758-9d22-794e63bc3875" "answer-87728be6-075d-537f-8aef-27d481efa7f0" "answer-41a234f5-7ea7-50f7-bbcb-7a8cfe94b9f8" "answer-13906513-b2f0-5250-9ebb-45ffb4a6b3ae" "answer-8bd1beb1-7b8d-5ba2-ad28-8ad264935383"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1905c358-05c8-5758-9d22-794e63bc3875" :answer/id #uuid "1905c358-05c8-5758-9d22-794e63bc3875" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87728be6-075d-537f-8aef-27d481efa7f0" :answer/id #uuid "87728be6-075d-537f-8aef-27d481efa7f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41a234f5-7ea7-50f7-bbcb-7a8cfe94b9f8" :answer/id #uuid "41a234f5-7ea7-50f7-bbcb-7a8cfe94b9f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13906513-b2f0-5250-9ebb-45ffb4a6b3ae" :answer/id #uuid "13906513-b2f0-5250-9ebb-45ffb4a6b3ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bd1beb1-7b8d-5ba2-ad28-8ad264935383" :answer/id #uuid "8bd1beb1-7b8d-5ba2-ad28-8ad264935383" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064528 :question/problem "$206-364=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $364$ is larger than $206,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n364-206\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,14\\end{aligned} \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n364-206=158.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n206-364=-158.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186061388 :answer-field/correct "answer-58dd9577-598d-5be3-9295-297a104810d9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58dd9577-598d-5be3-9295-297a104810d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58dd9577-598d-5be3-9295-297a104810d9" :answer/id #uuid "58dd9577-598d-5be3-9295-297a104810d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-158" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054800 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e800ccd8-93c4-50ec-b967-b7f8e3af90fc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e800ccd8-93c4-50ec-b967-b7f8e3af90fc" :question/id #uuid "e800ccd8-93c4-50ec-b967-b7f8e3af90fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-67032" :question/problem "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Twenty more than a number.\"" :question/worked-solution "If we denote our number by $a$, then the phrase \"twenty more than a number\" can be written as\n\n$$\na+20.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2567cecc-e540-571f-986b-6c5fcfdd8368"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2567cecc-e540-571f-986b-6c5fcfdd8368" :answer-field/id #uuid "2567cecc-e540-571f-986b-6c5fcfdd8368" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6c0f6c1d-30cb-5325-b1b4-4aae790a56f3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ece49a7a-6a81-5e2a-aa9b-c2756d56b63f" "answer-dcffd8c0-0654-5ce4-bfe4-e1f0bf668694" "answer-b3da9a63-8d40-5367-87c4-1d31dd79b916" "answer-155bdc41-9802-59b2-8bca-e743c38085f4" "answer-6c0f6c1d-30cb-5325-b1b4-4aae790a56f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ece49a7a-6a81-5e2a-aa9b-c2756d56b63f" :answer/id #uuid "ece49a7a-6a81-5e2a-aa9b-c2756d56b63f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20-a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcffd8c0-0654-5ce4-bfe4-e1f0bf668694" :answer/id #uuid "dcffd8c0-0654-5ce4-bfe4-e1f0bf668694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3da9a63-8d40-5367-87c4-1d31dd79b916" :answer/id #uuid "b3da9a63-8d40-5367-87c4-1d31dd79b916" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{a}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-155bdc41-9802-59b2-8bca-e743c38085f4" :answer/id #uuid "155bdc41-9802-59b2-8bca-e743c38085f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c0f6c1d-30cb-5325-b1b4-4aae790a56f3" :answer/id #uuid "6c0f6c1d-30cb-5325-b1b4-4aae790a56f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a+20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054807 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-785b3e3d-2e78-5863-9118-440c52c1081d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-785b3e3d-2e78-5863-9118-440c52c1081d" :question/id #uuid "785b3e3d-2e78-5863-9118-440c52c1081d" :question/math-academy-id "q-5754" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d43d45e070fe27d03717c2c88740b4536a23c7adba0ba2aa2ae451ecab34dbb5.png)\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point shown in the axes above?" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point is $5$ units to the *left* of the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $-5.$\n\nAdditionally, the point is $7$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has a $y$-coordinate of $-7.$\n\nThe point has an $x$-coordinate of $-5$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-7,$ so its coordinates are $(-5,-7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8fa81a20-3eba-5785-81ce-192978644ece"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8fa81a20-3eba-5785-81ce-192978644ece" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa81a20-3eba-5785-81ce-192978644ece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-47b7e555-339b-50e9-aaab-1a24dfc2973d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47b7e555-339b-50e9-aaab-1a24dfc2973d" "answer-77bd6183-b631-5c1e-a4b5-dbba0ddecd44" "answer-bb4f6388-69b6-5879-b082-4c5fb3cdbe9b" "answer-4ecfd91a-68ea-5d2d-b285-46f98c629e98" "answer-ff630284-77f1-5372-8795-b1017630bab6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47b7e555-339b-50e9-aaab-1a24dfc2973d" :answer/id #uuid "47b7e555-339b-50e9-aaab-1a24dfc2973d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,-7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77bd6183-b631-5c1e-a4b5-dbba0ddecd44" :answer/id #uuid "77bd6183-b631-5c1e-a4b5-dbba0ddecd44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb4f6388-69b6-5879-b082-4c5fb3cdbe9b" :answer/id #uuid "bb4f6388-69b6-5879-b082-4c5fb3cdbe9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ecfd91a-68ea-5d2d-b285-46f98c629e98" :answer/id #uuid "4ecfd91a-68ea-5d2d-b285-46f98c629e98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff630284-77f1-5372-8795-b1017630bab6" :answer/id #uuid "ff630284-77f1-5372-8795-b1017630bab6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152124 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e58a84f8-02f0-5e14-9a24-64165fe53601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e58a84f8-02f0-5e14-9a24-64165fe53601" :question/id #uuid "e58a84f8-02f0-5e14-9a24-64165fe53601" :question/math-academy-id "q-98374" :question/problem "Which of the following are natural numbers?\n\nI. $-\\frac{4}{3}$\n\nII. $3$\n\nIII. $-4$" :question/worked-solution "The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers.\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…\n$$\n\nOf the given numbers, $3$ is a natural number, but $-\\frac{4}{3}$ and $-4$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bddec77b-4bb5-5e2b-92e1-a0fa38b99c3e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bddec77b-4bb5-5e2b-92e1-a0fa38b99c3e" :answer-field/id #uuid "bddec77b-4bb5-5e2b-92e1-a0fa38b99c3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cea95e71-ceaf-544e-82f6-41c536fe741f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-42d46641-017d-5647-b920-cf17ddf92d65" "answer-e27ef853-fbbc-5693-b282-741e2f3dff09" "answer-d6be00ed-0b75-57c7-b788-a5b37ddea0cd" "answer-cea95e71-ceaf-544e-82f6-41c536fe741f" "answer-1f126447-987a-50d2-91b4-6bb6bc430b1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42d46641-017d-5647-b920-cf17ddf92d65" :answer/id #uuid "42d46641-017d-5647-b920-cf17ddf92d6