$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & =3\\,460-\\frac{1}{25}(250)^{2} \\\\  & =3\\,460-2\\,500 \\\\  & =960.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186202598 :answer-field/correct "answer-db5304b5-083a-506d-804d-17b1e72be0cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db5304b5-083a-506d-804d-17b1e72be0cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db5304b5-083a-506d-804d-17b1e72be0cd" :answer/id #uuid "db5304b5-083a-506d-804d-17b1e72be0cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "960" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-84b31519-3642-53d1-a74c-ac68de0d653b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-84b31519-3642-53d1-a74c-ac68de0d653b" :question/id #uuid "84b31519-3642-53d1-a74c-ac68de0d653b" :question/math-academy-id "q-251802" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $12$ | $4$ | $6$ | $10$ | $8$ | $15$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $20$ | $10$ | $5$ | $1$ | $7$ | $4$ | $9$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=535,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =12+4+6+10+8+15+11=66, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =20+10+5+1+7+4+9=56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=535.$\n\nFinally, by substituting in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=535-\\frac{1}{7}(66)(56)=535-528=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-15b52421-3d0b-5fa5-9d1e-da2b902cf171"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-15b52421-3d0b-5fa5-9d1e-da2b902cf171" :answer-field/id #uuid "15b52421-3d0b-5fa5-9d1e-da2b902cf171" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e2a6f16-31aa-5059-b5b0-f9450b74c6de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-489962a8-1deb-53b2-935a-d63467602030" "answer-ceb274b6-f1d2-5d6b-bab5-c50bfb7607a0" "answer-3558b18f-4849-5916-845e-fe6aa991a513" "answer-0e2a6f16-31aa-5059-b5b0-f9450b74c6de" "answer-d2ffdadb-e1e7-530b-b56a-cb1c31d4fe05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-489962a8-1deb-53b2-935a-d63467602030" :answer/id #uuid "489962a8-1deb-53b2-935a-d63467602030" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceb274b6-f1d2-5d6b-bab5-c50bfb7607a0" :answer/id #uuid "ceb274b6-f1d2-5d6b-bab5-c50bfb7607a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3558b18f-4849-5916-845e-fe6aa991a513" :answer/id #uuid "3558b18f-4849-5916-845e-fe6aa991a513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e2a6f16-31aa-5059-b5b0-f9450b74c6de" :answer/id #uuid "0e2a6f16-31aa-5059-b5b0-f9450b74c6de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2ffdadb-e1e7-530b-b56a-cb1c31d4fe05" :answer/id #uuid "d2ffdadb-e1e7-530b-b56a-cb1c31d4fe05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-094cdd1f-e814-5164-bdf6-dc0f3e0f507e" "question-1470b28d-5083-563f-9b26-d7812411f35b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-094cdd1f-e814-5164-bdf6-dc0f3e0f507e" :question/id #uuid "094cdd1f-e814-5164-bdf6-dc0f3e0f507e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251857" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $40$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{40},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{40}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=54,\\,{S}_{yy}=35,\\,{S}_{xy}=188.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=188.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{188}{40} \\\\  & =4.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f25616a1-e3e9-5a57-bef3-4345308333c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f25616a1-e3e9-5a57-bef3-4345308333c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f25616a1-e3e9-5a57-bef3-4345308333c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e38fe49d-81c4-5be4-8d42-66e01917801d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e38fe49d-81c4-5be4-8d42-66e01917801d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e38fe49d-81c4-5be4-8d42-66e01917801d" :answer/id #uuid "e38fe49d-81c4-5be4-8d42-66e01917801d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1470b28d-5083-563f-9b26-d7812411f35b" :question/id #uuid "1470b28d-5083-563f-9b26-d7812411f35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-251861" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $15$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{15},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{15}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=105,\\,{S}_{yy}=81,\\,{S}_{xy}=69.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=69.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{69}{15} \\\\  & =4.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-203627a4-892f-5453-bd75-4c6fd9a28c76"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-203627a4-892f-5453-bd75-4c6fd9a28c76" :answer-field/id #uuid "203627a4-892f-5453-bd75-4c6fd9a28c76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4f6a7f83-6364-5d0a-9fd6-ef7977380a2d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f6a7f83-6364-5d0a-9fd6-ef7977380a2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f6a7f83-6364-5d0a-9fd6-ef7977380a2d" :answer/id #uuid "4f6a7f83-6364-5d0a-9fd6-ef7977380a2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-26b0163b-edde-5aab-b2bd-a06d38a87337" :question/id #uuid "26b0163b-edde-5aab-b2bd-a06d38a87337" :question/math-academy-id "q-251898" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $8$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $9$ | $12$ | $10$ | $15$ | $12$ | $21$ | $6$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $4$ | $7$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{y}_{i}^{2}=144,$ calculate ${S}_{yy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${y}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{y}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${y}_{i}$ data:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{y}_{i}=3+4+5+4+7+2+3+4=32.\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{y}_{i}^{2}=144.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=144-\\frac{1}{8}(32)^{2}=144-128=16.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-97de8c2b-2160-5c30-92a5-23ff5b28889c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97de8c2b-2160-5c30-92a5-23ff5b28889c" :answer-field/id #uuid "97de8c2b-2160-5c30-92a5-23ff5b28889c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f3ad138-0924-5a40-8f81-cbba162c0f19" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba06e549-bfbb-5699-a72e-3e553bcf6f6e" "answer-8f3ad138-0924-5a40-8f81-cbba162c0f19" "answer-f4353feb-c770-5137-9c93-96535a82b4a0" "answer-b647c1b2-e8a2-513d-bca8-1ba7556ab769" "answer-66aa0cf4-9fdd-5d95-be6b-811b502b95a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba06e549-bfbb-5699-a72e-3e553bcf6f6e" :answer/id #uuid "ba06e549-bfbb-5699-a72e-3e553bcf6f6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f3ad138-0924-5a40-8f81-cbba162c0f19" :answer/id #uuid "8f3ad138-0924-5a40-8f81-cbba162c0f19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4353feb-c770-5137-9c93-96535a82b4a0" :answer/id #uuid "f4353feb-c770-5137-9c93-96535a82b4a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b647c1b2-e8a2-513d-bca8-1ba7556ab769" :answer/id #uuid "b647c1b2-e8a2-513d-bca8-1ba7556ab769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=21.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66aa0cf4-9fdd-5d95-be6b-811b502b95a8" :answer/id #uuid "66aa0cf4-9fdd-5d95-be6b-811b502b95a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7aa8c243-9cf9-5efe-a839-52140fca9bde" :activity/id #uuid "7aa8c243-9cf9-5efe-a839-52140fca9bde" :activity/title "Sums of Squares" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050406 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-7802b9e3-fd31-5e80-8ab7-f1535e9dbf56" "step-5d03f414-94f2-58bc-a50f-eb3425afa07a" "step-b37e6950-25d6-5437-bec0-c80cada70611" "step-c7b1248b-f25e-5efc-bec5-63e8214005ee" "step-ae51bedd-deee-5ef3-b5f9-595f36d08dbe"] :activity/first-step "step-7802b9e3-fd31-5e80-8ab7-f1535e9dbf56" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7802b9e3-fd31-5e80-8ab7-f1535e9dbf56" :step/id #uuid "7802b9e3-fd31-5e80-8ab7-f1535e9dbf56" :step/content 17592186204442 :step/next "step-5d03f414-94f2-58bc-a50f-eb3425afa07a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5d03f414-94f2-58bc-a50f-eb3425afa07a" :step/id #uuid "5d03f414-94f2-58bc-a50f-eb3425afa07a" :step/content "question-84b31519-3642-53d1-a74c-ac68de0d653b" :step/next "step-b37e6950-25d6-5437-bec0-c80cada70611" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b37e6950-25d6-5437-bec0-c80cada70611" :step/id #uuid "b37e6950-25d6-5437-bec0-c80cada70611" :step/content "question-094cdd1f-e814-5164-bdf6-dc0f3e0f507e" :step/next "step-c7b1248b-f25e-5efc-bec5-63e8214005ee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c7b1248b-f25e-5efc-bec5-63e8214005ee" :step/id #uuid "c7b1248b-f25e-5efc-bec5-63e8214005ee" :step/content "question-1470b28d-5083-563f-9b26-d7812411f35b" :step/next "step-ae51bedd-deee-5ef3-b5f9-595f36d08dbe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ae51bedd-deee-5ef3-b5f9-595f36d08dbe" :step/id #uuid "ae51bedd-deee-5ef3-b5f9-595f36d08dbe" :step/content "question-26b0163b-edde-5aab-b2bd-a06d38a87337" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064382 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-15178b94-38d6-597d-bc8c-39fd354b56c7" "question-0fa1eef6-69ad-599c-9e20-68839bce41b1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064383 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2bda6d09-1af6-5a1c-86e9-4f34148c24fa" "question-44d55ece-0880-515f-a521-353e6c740d6b" "question-385d74bf-db85-520e-88d9-f555fc3d02fe"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-15178b94-38d6-597d-bc8c-39fd354b56c7" :question/id #uuid "15178b94-38d6-597d-bc8c-39fd354b56c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-2588" :question/problem "![](images/77/7741295c73895ec39933adec100c9f3fc7e803fa8ea2a02dae543477c45cbea4.png)\n\nA boat $B$ is being pulled in toward a dock $D$ with a rope by a fisherman $F$ standing on the dock. His hands are $4\\text{ ft}$ above the ground, and he is pulling the rope at a rate of $3\\text{ ft/s}$, how fast is the distance between the dock and the boat decreasing when the boat is $3\\text{ft}$ from the dock?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/af/afbe02b63ca4d45ae4d1759d7fa452b57a8b43f073d08b1368f51472e2e4ea8b.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between the dock and the boat,\n\n- $y$ is the distance between the fisherman's hands and the ground, and\n\n- $z$ is the distance between the fisherman's hands and the boat mooring.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $x,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ \n\nWe know that $x=3\\,\\text{ft}$ and $y=4\\,\\text{ft }.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =9+16 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =25 \\\\ z & =5\\,\\text{ft}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=-3\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{h},$\n\n- the distance between the fisherman's hands and the ground remains the same, so $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=0.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(3)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(4)(0) & =2(5)(-3) \\\\ 6\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-30 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the dock and the boat is decreasing at a rate of $5\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5295ec83-ed80-5552-9033-ebac568bd564"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5295ec83-ed80-5552-9033-ebac568bd564" :answer-field/id #uuid "5295ec83-ed80-5552-9033-ebac568bd564" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-072e352e-d8d1-59a7-b841-bd241577a866" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bef19881-ffaa-50b7-be8d-4595b18c0067" "answer-2900f8e2-5f65-5ee6-9082-48e9d9465465" "answer-072e352e-d8d1-59a7-b841-bd241577a866" "answer-94f4bb0d-5e3b-51da-bf7f-0da6c8573a76" "answer-3a07a3c6-0949-52af-ae18-a7560b5c11e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bef19881-ffaa-50b7-be8d-4595b18c0067" :answer/id #uuid "bef19881-ffaa-50b7-be8d-4595b18c0067" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2900f8e2-5f65-5ee6-9082-48e9d9465465" :answer/id #uuid "2900f8e2-5f65-5ee6-9082-48e9d9465465" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-072e352e-d8d1-59a7-b841-bd241577a866" :answer/id #uuid "072e352e-d8d1-59a7-b841-bd241577a866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94f4bb0d-5e3b-51da-bf7f-0da6c8573a76" :answer/id #uuid "94f4bb0d-5e3b-51da-bf7f-0da6c8573a76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a07a3c6-0949-52af-ae18-a7560b5c11e4" :answer/id #uuid "3a07a3c6-0949-52af-ae18-a7560b5c11e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0fa1eef6-69ad-599c-9e20-68839bce41b1" :question/id #uuid "0fa1eef6-69ad-599c-9e20-68839bce41b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49014" :question/problem "![](images/35/3556e6b8bda17ab8242b8cd7924e1f5ad975efcbc6c5235667d786b2f0908e1d.png)\n\nTrain $A$ travels east from station $S$ at a constant velocity of $153\\,\\text{km/h},$ and train $B$ travels south toward $S.$ The distance between the trains is increasing at a rate of $35\\text{ km/h}.$  What is the speed of train $B$ when train $A$ is $51\\,\\text{km}$ from the station and train $B$ is $68\\,\\text{km}$ from the station?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/81/81d16bb54bdecca628d769cd08d02dd327c5483851c2421fb595446c34f8a124.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between the station and train $A,$\n\n- $y$ is the distance between the station and train $B,$\n\n- $z$ is the distance between the two trains.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $y,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ \n\nWe know that $x=51\\,\\text{km}$ and $y=68\\,\\text{km}.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {51}^{2}+{68}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =7\\,225 \\\\ z & =85\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=153\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h},$\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=35\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(51)(153)+2(68)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(85)(35) \\\\ 136\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =5\\,950-15\\,606 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{9\\,656}{136} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-71.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of train $B$ is $71\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b19ef90c-29be-517a-8b07-95053303a6ae"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b19ef90c-29be-517a-8b07-95053303a6ae" :answer-field/id #uuid "b19ef90c-29be-517a-8b07-95053303a6ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3dfb70c6-f15d-5a56-96ae-62a357522691" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47114b29-8ab3-5f62-9aa5-c467498f9b12" "answer-e0588013-71dd-515f-af8c-61faea7d5d46" "answer-3dfb70c6-f15d-5a56-96ae-62a357522691" "answer-981ee76f-3c96-5cf7-a94f-a1f50bafb998" "answer-bcf8f1d8-5f56-5238-805c-44a612087016"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47114b29-8ab3-5f62-9aa5-c467498f9b12" :answer/id #uuid "47114b29-8ab3-5f62-9aa5-c467498f9b12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "142\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0588013-71dd-515f-af8c-61faea7d5d46" :answer/id #uuid "e0588013-71dd-515f-af8c-61faea7d5d46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "710\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3dfb70c6-f15d-5a56-96ae-62a357522691" :answer/id #uuid "3dfb70c6-f15d-5a56-96ae-62a357522691" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "71\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-981ee76f-3c96-5cf7-a94f-a1f50bafb998" :answer/id #uuid "981ee76f-3c96-5cf7-a94f-a1f50bafb998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{71}{2}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcf8f1d8-5f56-5238-805c-44a612087016" :answer/id #uuid "bcf8f1d8-5f56-5238-805c-44a612087016" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{71}{3}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bda6d09-1af6-5a1c-86e9-4f34148c24fa" :question/id #uuid "2bda6d09-1af6-5a1c-86e9-4f34148c24fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-104079" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dbee02f0c07041dd8424faf683952ada2f7f1a604f9bf89a65588eaf3b6f9f6.png)\n\nThe legs of an isosceles right triangle are increasing. The length, measured in feet, of each leg is given by $x(t)=t+{t}^{2},$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. What is the rate of the change of the length of the hypotenuse after $2$ seconds? Give your answer rounded to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "In the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the length of the equal sides, and\n\n- $z$ is the length of the hypotenuse.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $x,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $z,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nFirst, we determine the length of the equal sides after $2$ seconds. We get \n\n$$\nx=x(2)=(2)+(2)^{2}=6\\text{ ft}.\n$$\n\nWe can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{x}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {6}^{2}+{6}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 72 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ z & ≈8.485\\,3\\,\\text{ft}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe rate of change of the sides is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}={x}^{′}(t)=2t+1.$ So, when $t=2$ their velocity is\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}={x}^{′}(2)=2(2)+1=5\\text{ ft/s}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(6)(5)+2(6)(5) & ≈2(8.485\\,3)\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & ≈7.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hypotenuse's length is changing at a rate of $7.1\\text{ ft/s}$ after $2$ seconds." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aab01a3c-9c95-5b30-9a80-de234df6bc12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aab01a3c-9c95-5b30-9a80-de234df6bc12" :answer-field/id #uuid "aab01a3c-9c95-5b30-9a80-de234df6bc12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c303aadb-c779-5586-a605-55e86f1bc278" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8769679e-53c2-5284-875f-0b62a16bd910" "answer-8db4ecb8-a27a-582a-ba29-b2b279bd5866" "answer-31136b91-ada4-5499-9ab7-4a99b8df1106" "answer-770caf56-2690-584a-b68e-89f941399a82" "answer-c303aadb-c779-5586-a605-55e86f1bc278"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8769679e-53c2-5284-875f-0b62a16bd910" :answer/id #uuid "8769679e-53c2-5284-875f-0b62a16bd910" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.0\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8db4ecb8-a27a-582a-ba29-b2b279bd5866" :answer/id #uuid "8db4ecb8-a27a-582a-ba29-b2b279bd5866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.2\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31136b91-ada4-5499-9ab7-4a99b8df1106" :answer/id #uuid "31136b91-ada4-5499-9ab7-4a99b8df1106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.7\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-770caf56-2690-584a-b68e-89f941399a82" :answer/id #uuid "770caf56-2690-584a-b68e-89f941399a82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.1\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c303aadb-c779-5586-a605-55e86f1bc278" :answer/id #uuid "c303aadb-c779-5586-a605-55e86f1bc278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.1\\text{ ft/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-44d55ece-0880-515f-a521-353e6c740d6b" :question/id #uuid "44d55ece-0880-515f-a521-353e6c740d6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-2942" :question/problem "The length of one leg of a right triangle increases at the rate of $3\\text{ m/s},$ while the length of the second leg is decreasing at the rate of $2\\text{ m/s}.$ How fast is the length of the hypotenuse changing when the length of the increasing leg is $12\\text{ m}$ and the length of the decreasing leg is $16\\text{ m}?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by drawing a diagram of the problem.\n\n![](images/ee/eee3de464da57671142e2677974b44c63dc2397215ffdd2aa36e2c3d401a647d.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the length of the increasing side,\n\n- $y$ is the length of the decreasing side,\n\n- $z$ is the length of the hypotenuse.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $z,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}.$ \n\nWe know that $x=12\\,\\text{m}$ and $y=16\\,\\text{m}.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {12}^{2}+{16}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 400 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ z & =20\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $x=12\\,\\text{m}$ and $y=16\\,\\text{m},$\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=-2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$  when $x=12\\,\\text{m}$ and $y=16\\,\\text{m}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(12)(3)+2(16)(-2) & =2(20)\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 8 & =40\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{8}{40} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the hypotenuse is changing at a rate of $\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-447900b5-91db-51d6-8acb-33c461630cf8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-447900b5-91db-51d6-8acb-33c461630cf8" :answer-field/id #uuid "447900b5-91db-51d6-8acb-33c461630cf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-af8f3c25-8d64-51cb-9a3d-fbb1ab8563c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-777dae30-3e3c-5423-b450-e06b7c17385d" "answer-3da9ef0d-595c-584c-bf88-ab4b724d3cd9" "answer-af8f3c25-8d64-51cb-9a3d-fbb1ab8563c0" "answer-2c37f289-4fa3-5f30-a819-93edd8808892" "answer-d98c6aa5-05dd-5715-87aa-fa3f5ae0f286"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-777dae30-3e3c-5423-b450-e06b7c17385d" :answer/id #uuid "777dae30-3e3c-5423-b450-e06b7c17385d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3da9ef0d-595c-584c-bf88-ab4b724d3cd9" :answer/id #uuid "3da9ef0d-595c-584c-bf88-ab4b724d3cd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af8f3c25-8d64-51cb-9a3d-fbb1ab8563c0" :answer/id #uuid "af8f3c25-8d64-51cb-9a3d-fbb1ab8563c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c37f289-4fa3-5f30-a819-93edd8808892" :answer/id #uuid "2c37f289-4fa3-5f30-a819-93edd8808892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d98c6aa5-05dd-5715-87aa-fa3f5ae0f286" :answer/id #uuid "d98c6aa5-05dd-5715-87aa-fa3f5ae0f286" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}\\text{ m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-385d74bf-db85-520e-88d9-f555fc3d02fe" :question/id #uuid "385d74bf-db85-520e-88d9-f555fc3d02fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-104077" :question/problem "After attending school, Elizabeth and Jessica leave at the same time. Elizabeth heads north at a speed of $4.5\\text{ mph},$ while Jessica heads east at a speed of $6\\text{ mph}.$ How fast are the two moving away from each other after walking for $2$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "We start by drawing a diagram of the problem.\n\n![](images/2b/2b012a853cf973cc68df35bbd94a498fd1d0d907548c1f6d8ca3f842c967c877.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between Jessica and the school,\n\n- $y$ is the distance between Elizabeth and the school, and\n\n- $z$ is the distance between Elizabeth and Jessica.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $z,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nFirst, we determine Elizabeth's distance from school and Jessica's distance from school after $2$ hours. Since their velocities are constants, we get \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot t=4.5(2)=9\\text{ mi}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot t=6(2)=12\\text{ mi}.\n$$\n\nWe can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {9}^{2}+{12}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 225 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ z & =15\\,\\text{mi}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=4.5\\,\\text{mph}$ after $2$ hours,\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=6\\,\\text{mph}$ after $2$ hours.\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(9)(4.5)+2(12)(6) & =2(15)\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 225 & =30\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between Elizabeth and Jessica increases at a rate of $7.5\\,\\text{mph}$ after walking $2$ hours." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2979a513-9e50-5580-a324-a6d842e9ce90"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2979a513-9e50-5580-a324-a6d842e9ce90" :answer-field/id #uuid "2979a513-9e50-5580-a324-a6d842e9ce90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-79307c51-6bb8-5bf4-add1-639696a73890" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2041b6e3-2c7b-5767-bee7-c0917fa37089" "answer-f57c07c6-710c-5e34-b6d0-e037d5b35912" "answer-79307c51-6bb8-5bf4-add1-639696a73890" "answer-5a4b991b-0be0-5421-81c6-155a8e77ad74" "answer-7a90aea4-90dd-561b-8cfe-71c7cd68506b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2041b6e3-2c7b-5767-bee7-c0917fa37089" :answer/id #uuid "2041b6e3-2c7b-5767-bee7-c0917fa37089" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\text{mph}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f57c07c6-710c-5e34-b6d0-e037d5b35912" :answer/id #uuid "f57c07c6-710c-5e34-b6d0-e037d5b35912" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{mph}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79307c51-6bb8-5bf4-add1-639696a73890" :answer/id #uuid "79307c51-6bb8-5bf4-add1-639696a73890" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5\\,\\text{mph}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a4b991b-0be0-5421-81c6-155a8e77ad74" :answer/id #uuid "5a4b991b-0be0-5421-81c6-155a8e77ad74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{mph}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a90aea4-90dd-561b-8cfe-71c7cd68506b" :answer/id #uuid "7a90aea4-90dd-561b-8cfe-71c7cd68506b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\text{mph}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064436 :activity/expected-seconds 1140.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d61adfc9-5b12-5408-9a76-aa7eede82be4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134226 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrices $P$ and $Q?$\n\nI. $Q$ is invertible\n\nII. $PQ$ is always orthogonal\n\nIII. $P+Q$ is always orthogonal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The inverse of an orthogonal matrix $Q$ is given by ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the product $(PQ)\\cdot (PQ)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(PQ)\\cdot (PQ)^{T} & =PQ\\cdot {Q}^{T}{P}^{T} \\\\  & =P(Q{Q}^{T}){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P(I){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P{P}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, consider the following sum of two orthogonal matrices:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe resulting matrix is not orthogonal since, for example,it is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131395 :answer-field/correct 17592186131397 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-d61adfc9-5b12-5408-9a76-aa7eede82be4" :question/id #uuid "d61adfc9-5b12-5408-9a76-aa7eede82be4" :question/math-academy-id "q-41715" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $Q?$\n\nI. $Q{Q}^{T}=I$\n\nII. ${Q}^{2}$ is the zero matrix\n\nIII. If $A=QB{Q}^{-1}$ then $|det(A)|=|det(B)|$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true.\nIt's true by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false. Let's consider the identity matrix\n\n$$\nQ=I=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that $Q$ is an orthogonal matrix and also ${Q}^{2}=Q\\ne O.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Computing $|det(A)|,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(A)| & =|det(QB{Q}^{-1})| \\\\  & =|det(QB{Q}^{T})| \\\\  & =|det(Q)|\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot |det({Q}^{T})| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|det(B)|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e9d10573-cd86-5734-a745-dadd21dc2271"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e9d10573-cd86-5734-a745-dadd21dc2271" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9d10573-cd86-5734-a745-dadd21dc2271" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b2930480-2eb9-594e-9c28-dd13242c011e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a32d8fdf-be70-57b2-8de9-9bbc2f2e4992" "answer-297ecca7-1d04-565f-97fa-4bf34f030962" "answer-b2930480-2eb9-594e-9c28-dd13242c011e" "answer-38cd3098-2a5e-55de-9315-3b8f18a09933" "answer-98bf55fb-3a39-5303-9541-a60e5da17d4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a32d8fdf-be70-57b2-8de9-9bbc2f2e4992" :answer/id #uuid "a32d8fdf-be70-57b2-8de9-9bbc2f2e4992" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-297ecca7-1d04-565f-97fa-4bf34f030962" :answer/id #uuid "297ecca7-1d04-565f-97fa-4bf34f030962" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2930480-2eb9-594e-9c28-dd13242c011e" :answer/id #uuid "b2930480-2eb9-594e-9c28-dd13242c011e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38cd3098-2a5e-55de-9315-3b8f18a09933" :answer/id #uuid "38cd3098-2a5e-55de-9315-3b8f18a09933" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98bf55fb-3a39-5303-9541-a60e5da17d4b" :answer/id #uuid "98bf55fb-3a39-5303-9541-a60e5da17d4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-40997d44-940a-52f1-8654-3ad1000fd7b5" :activity/id #uuid "40997d44-940a-52f1-8654-3ad1000fd7b5" :activity/title "Orthogonal Matrices" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049606 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-057e2df5-62de-5772-a9be-1e31132f5c72" "step-a0dd7217-b8aa-50b8-a492-e108a3a2b002" "step-734bd8c7-6cda-5908-8980-183fb1942573" "step-8d0835ae-d91c-5c36-b4d2-e4d86cb27fd8" "step-5c859452-c242-51fd-8f27-755ab3b53b24"] :activity/first-step "step-057e2df5-62de-5772-a9be-1e31132f5c72" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-057e2df5-6