 \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the predicate is $9<3.$ Since $9$ is not less than $3,$ the predicate is false. Therefore,\n\n$$\n1[9<3]=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cbbe48f6-f510-548a-9eb2-bcc76f4b3d7f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cbbe48f6-f510-548a-9eb2-bcc76f4b3d7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbbe48f6-f510-548a-9eb2-bcc76f4b3d7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0d31ae15-4799-5dcb-b0de-9552c9af5297" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d31ae15-4799-5dcb-b0de-9552c9af5297" "answer-beeabc21-ba82-5dc1-b8aa-50cd9eb8eb34" "answer-61a0a683-cee4-5ee5-8382-168325ade50d" "answer-34dba6bf-e41e-5f62-8f3f-cd44ea2f03d2" "answer-2f80aa26-406f-5364-b5bb-d75a8b6a927a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d31ae15-4799-5dcb-b0de-9552c9af5297" :answer/id #uuid "0d31ae15-4799-5dcb-b0de-9552c9af5297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-beeabc21-ba82-5dc1-b8aa-50cd9eb8eb34" :answer/id #uuid "beeabc21-ba82-5dc1-b8aa-50cd9eb8eb34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61a0a683-cee4-5ee5-8382-168325ade50d" :answer/id #uuid "61a0a683-cee4-5ee5-8382-168325ade50d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34dba6bf-e41e-5f62-8f3f-cd44ea2f03d2" :answer/id #uuid "34dba6bf-e41e-5f62-8f3f-cd44ea2f03d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f80aa26-406f-5364-b5bb-d75a8b6a927a" :answer/id #uuid "2f80aa26-406f-5364-b5bb-d75a8b6a927a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1501d1dd-a30a-5622-a170-02307bfe9a8b" :question/id #uuid "1501d1dd-a30a-5622-a170-02307bfe9a8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-346657" :question/problem "Evaluate the indicator function\n$1[7\\in \\{2,4,6,10\\}].$" :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the predicate is $7\\in \\{2,4,6,10\\}.$ Since $7$ is not an element of the set $\\{2,4,6,10\\},$ the predicate is false. Therefore,\n\n$$\n1[7\\in \\{2,4,6,10\\}]=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74f1f48a-399d-5f1e-8444-768471429caf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74f1f48a-399d-5f1e-8444-768471429caf" :answer-field/id #uuid "74f1f48a-399d-5f1e-8444-768471429caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8fd3549b-2060-5e8f-9079-20bc1ec9c8cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8fd3549b-2060-5e8f-9079-20bc1ec9c8cd" "answer-7e48777f-ff2d-592c-b304-61e39dd2f866" "answer-6913e577-51fe-515b-8665-cfebf3c44f81" "answer-4323438d-d075-5cf2-8dc1-6b1709d1a612" "answer-24907d49-66d4-50cb-a4c8-3543263283e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fd3549b-2060-5e8f-9079-20bc1ec9c8cd" :answer/id #uuid "8fd3549b-2060-5e8f-9079-20bc1ec9c8cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e48777f-ff2d-592c-b304-61e39dd2f866" :answer/id #uuid "7e48777f-ff2d-592c-b304-61e39dd2f866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6913e577-51fe-515b-8665-cfebf3c44f81" :answer/id #uuid "6913e577-51fe-515b-8665-cfebf3c44f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4323438d-d075-5cf2-8dc1-6b1709d1a612" :answer/id #uuid "4323438d-d075-5cf2-8dc1-6b1709d1a612" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24907d49-66d4-50cb-a4c8-3543263283e6" :answer/id #uuid "24907d49-66d4-50cb-a4c8-3543263283e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ee0e20b3-c728-5a30-b95b-8f191603cec6" :question/id #uuid "ee0e20b3-c728-5a30-b95b-8f191603cec6" :question/math-academy-id "q-351129" :question/problem "Let $E=\\{0,4,8,12\\}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to $1[10\\in E]?$" :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of a set $A$ equals $1$ if $x\\in A$ and $0$ if $x\\notin A.$ This can be written using Iverson bracket notation as\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=1[x\\in A].\n$$\n\nHere, the Iverson bracket expression $1[10\\in E]$ has $x=10$ and $A=E.$ Therefore, converting back to set indicator notation, we have\n\n$$\n1[10\\in E]={1}_{E}(10).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ac89a69-ed84-581a-8ccb-a1473c225f7f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ac89a69-ed84-581a-8ccb-a1473c225f7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac89a69-ed84-581a-8ccb-a1473c225f7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1b433f0e-c20a-56a6-be38-54b150ce736d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-63e3e50d-5a21-5132-9d32-2e33146bdd1a" "answer-9e322a5e-ed05-52c1-a8dd-53596804e29d" "answer-1b433f0e-c20a-56a6-be38-54b150ce736d" "answer-ddb2ddd0-6040-5f09-a90c-68bb2cebbdc8" "answer-6d2b534e-ad9a-51c7-9f08-07e0e3f70ca9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63e3e50d-5a21-5132-9d32-2e33146bdd1a" :answer/id #uuid "63e3e50d-5a21-5132-9d32-2e33146bdd1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1}_{10}(0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e322a5e-ed05-52c1-a8dd-53596804e29d" :a